In article <1991Feb19.205631.15341@chinet.chi.il.us> prb@chinet.chi.il.us (Paul Botts) writes:

>5) There should be a way to get an inventory list of all the items in a
>pile you`re standing on.

Um, what's wrong with ":"?

>6) When you try to wield, wear, put on, take off, remove, eat, apply,
>read, quaff, zap, Zap, throw something, the list of the appropriate
>items in your pack should be automatically displayed (like if you done
>I-whatever). This could be an option which could be turned off by people
>annoyed by it, but the default should be ON.

You can get this by answering "?" to the prompt about what to eat,
apply, etc. I'd rather not see the list when I know what I want. Minor quibble:
the list in response to ? doesn't show you everything it is legit to
apply the command to. That is, zap shows wands, read shows spellbooks and
scrools, so far so good, but throw shows only weapons (i'd prefer weapons,
gems (I throw rocks) and food). And why can't you throw gold?

My two big choices for interface changes: 

(1) flush the keyboard buffer
at certain well defined points, to reduce the chance of smacking into
things you'd rather not hit, or improve the various "go a long way" keys,
or have a status light saying "I am processing some keystrokes from you"
so that I don't put two many keys in.

(2) Have an option (like PICKUP) about the displaying of the contents
of every square you step on. So annoying on crowded levels with little
piles of stuff every few steps to have to stop and be told about it.
One of the lovely things about levitating is the game no longer assumes
you stop and root through every pile of stuff, including stuff you just
rooted through five minutes ago. I'd call this option LOOK, and I'd have
it work just like pickup (simple keystroke to toggle, default ON, can
be set in options file). When I care, I can look with :, just as I can pick
up with ,.

